The collector's rewrite of LLVM IR that -emit-llvm-bc wrote, read back as
text, which a test can then edit by hand: the bitcode keeps the root types'
notes and says it is optimized, so the read-back module compiles to the
same object file as the source, and -fdebug-dump-statepoints shows the same
rewrite from either.

RUN: merkc -fc1 -O2 -emit-obj %S/../statepoints.m -o %t.source.o
RUN: merkc -fc1 -O2 -emit-llvm-bc %S/../statepoints.m -o %t.bc
RUN: llvm-dis %t.bc -o %t.ll
RUN: merkc -fc1 -O2 -emit-obj %t.ll -o %t.read-back.o
RUN: cmp %t.source.o %t.read-back.o
RUN: merkc -fc1 -O2 -fdebug-dump-statepoints %S/../statepoints.m -o - | FileCheck %s
RUN: merkc -fc1 -O2 -fdebug-dump-statepoints %t.ll -o - | FileCheck %s
CHECK: gc.statepoint
CHECK: gc.relocate

What else the IR can be compiled to.
RUN: not merkc -fc1 -emit-merk %t.ll 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONLY
ONLY: LLVM IR input can only be compiled to LLVM IR, bitcode, statepoints, assembly or an object file
